    "body": "The current copy reader admits only exact current-token recurrences and compares shallow equality/eight-slot features. Calibrating its output would leave the project's learned geometric-attention hypothesis largely untested. This change selects learned causal query/source descriptions and directed finite H4 relationships as the next primary experiment, with a repaired/calibrated PR #1314 reader as comparator and loss-based NoRead/copy strength in both arms.\n\nThe single new execution prompt binds that experiment to exact memory, shared candidate support for ranking comparisons, preserved exact-key information when broadening admission, causal features, representation-independent targets, generated behavior and full access cost. The previous memory-utility-only prompt redirects to it. The canonical five-stage roadmap now explicitly connects relational access, structural persistence, dependent composition, broad language/executed Rust, and efficient API/WASM/Studio delivery. The reduced Hopf/spin relation is exercised now; full S7/E8/harmonic state remains conditional on an identified need.\n\nThe completed DeepSeek handoff is reconciled with the same delivered PR #1314, not counted as a new run. Its fitter already contained737 read and515 NoRead examples. The audit preserves the synthetic-margin amplitude rationale, corrects the implied absence of negative supervision, and derives bounded one-step copy utility without claiming new model performance. README, roadmap, project map, current state, direction and continuation are synchronized; original sealed evidence is unchanged.\n\nValidation: source and saved admission/amplitude receipts inspected; PR #1314 head/merge have identical tree945f2bdd4ab6f2fa7af7683dad9163887a96da11; independent evidence/math/source reviews of the final mechanism decision; `git diff --check`; claim-wording check;683 local Markdown targets resolve. No Rust edit, build, fit, model forward, ledger mutation or deletion. Free-space snapshot approximately50.1GB/46.7GiB; owner/research worktrees preserved. Queue compatibility acknowledgements are not tests.\n\nReferences #973, #820, #1139, #962, #963, #964.\n",
